Brent J. Nordquist wrote:

> 1. Are there any monsters that will loot my stash if I don't lock it?
> Any advantage to using a chest vs. a large box?

There aren't. No monster can open a bag or chest. There's no difference 
between any container in this regard (bag, sack, chest, box).

Note that a box will also protect your stuff from gelatinous cubes: they 
will eat the box, but the contents won't be digested by them, just 
swallowed.

> 2. Prayer timeout: I've seen lots of references that there is one, but
> how do you calculate the actual value?

You can't. The random factor is too large to make calculations possible.

> 3. Tossing food at monsters (ponies/horses/etc.) can make them
> "peaceful" but is it possible to make them "tame" on food alone, or
> do you need charm monster/taming magic?

You need to throw food they like. Quadruped like vegetables, cats and 
dogs like meat.

> 4. Rusted/burnt and corroded/rotted: Are these "erosion" damages
> somehow paired the way I've listed them here? I know about reading
> enchant armor/weapon while confused, and that !oOil restores rusted
> and corroded items... any other way to restore burnt and rotted items?

Not that I know of.

> 5. I've seen references to naming one's weapons Sting or Orcrist; what
> does that do? (I use daggers.)

You may name an *elven* dagger or broadsword "Sting" or "Orcrist", 
respectively.

> 6. I know some of the dangers of turn-to-stone corpses. *trice corpses
> (even blessed ones) rot away over time; any way to preserve them?

I think corpses rot less fast when you bless them.

> Was I imagining it, or did a *trice corpse I put in an oilskin sack
> later turn into a copper spellbook?

You were imagining it.

